.TH MINIT 1 "1970-1-1" "v1.0" "Custom Scripts Manual"
.SH NAME
minit \- CMake project initializer and dependency manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B minit
\fIinit\fR|\fIinitialize\fR|\fInew\fR [\fB\-v\fR] \fIpath\fR [\fB\-n\fR \fINAME\fR] [\fB\-l\fR] [\fB\-b\fR] [\fB\-c\fR] [\fB\-\-cc\fR] [\fB\-\-cxx\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-c\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-git\fR] [\fB\-\-tests\fR] [\fB\-\-pkg\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-nix\fR]
.br
.B minit
\fIconf\fR|\fIconfigure\fR \fIpath\fR [\fB\-\-add\fR \fIdep\fR [\fB\-\-static\fR] [\fB\-\-public\fR|\fB\-\-private\fR]] [\fB\-\-remove\fR \fIdep\fR]
.br
.B minit
\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B minit
is a utility script for initializing and managing CMake projects. It creates structured project directories, handles dependency management through a unified interface, and optionally supports Nix flake generation.
.SH INIT OPTIONS
The following options are available in \fIinit\fR mode:
.TP
.B \-n, \-\-name \fINAME\fR
Specify a custom project name. Defaults to the directory name.
.TP
.B \-l, \-\-lib
Mark the project as a library. This enables the generation of shared/static targets and an \fIinclude\fR directory.
.TP
.B \-b, \-\-no\-bin
Disable the generation of a binary executable target.
.TP
.B \-c, \-\-config
Generate a \fBconfigure\fR wrapper script. This script provides a standard interface to CMake configuration and build directory management.
.TP
.B \-\-cc
Enable the generation of \fBcompile_commands.json\fR (via \fBCMAKE_EXPORT_COMPILE_COMMANDS\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-cxx
Enable C++ language support (adds CXX to project languages and glob patterns).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-c
Disable C language support.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-git
Do not initialize a git repository or generate \fB.gitignore\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-tests
Enable testing infrastructure. Creates a \fBtests\fR directory, generates a CMake test configuration, and enables CTest.
.TP
.B \-\-pkg\-config
Enable PkgConfig validation. Dependencies added later will be checked via PkgConfig by default.
.TP
.B \-\-nix
Generate \fBflake.nix\fR and \fBpackage.nix\fR files. This allows the project to be built and developed within a Nix environment.

.SH CONF OPTIONS
The following options are available in \fIconf\fR mode to manage dependencies:
.TP
\fB\-\-add \fIdep\fR
Add a dependency to the project.
.RS
.IP \(bu 4
\fB\-\-static\fR: Forces static linking. If PkgConfig is used, it adds the \fBSTATIC\fR flag to the module check. If not, it wraps the dependency in linker-specific static flags (non-MSVC).
.IP \(bu 4
\fB\-\-public\fR: Links the dependency to the \fBdeps_public\fR interface. (Default for libraries).
.IP \(bu 4
\fB\-\-private\fR: Links the dependency to the \fBdeps_private\fR interface. (Default for binaries).
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-remove \fIdep\fR
Remove a dependency from the \fBdeps_public\fR or \fBdeps_private\fR interface and clean up associated PkgConfig checks.

.SH DEPENDENCY MANAGEMENT
Dependencies are managed via two interface targets in \fICMakeLists.txt\fR: \fBdeps_public\fR and \fBdeps_private\fR.
.PP
The \fBconf\fR mode automatically modifies \fICMakeLists.txt\fR using \fBsed\fR to insert:
.IP 1.
\fBpkg_check_modules\fR (if PkgConfig is detected/enabled).
.IP 2.
\fBtarget_link_libraries\fR for the appropriate interface target.
.PP
Manual marker comments (e.g., @DEPS_START@) are not used; the script inserts commands dynamically based on existing file content.

.SH NIX INTEGRATION
If the project was initialized with \fB\-\-nix\fR (or manually contains a \fBpackage.nix\fR), the \fBconf\fR mode will attempt to keep the Nix expressions in sync.
.PP
When adding a dependency via \fB\-\-add\fR:
.IP \(bu 4
The script checks if the package exists in \fBnixpkgs\fR (requires \fBnix\fR command).
.IP \(bu 4
If found, it adds the package to the \fBbuildInputs\fR list in \fBpackage.nix\fR.
.PP
When removing a dependency via \fB\-\-remove\fR, it is removed from \fBpackage.nix\fR.

.SH EXAMPLES
Initialize a C++ library with Nix support:
.RS
.PP
minit init ./mylib \-\-lib \-\-cxx \-\-nix
.RE
.PP
Add a static dependency using PkgConfig:
.RS
.PP
minit conf ./mylib \-\-add zlib \-\-static \-\-public
.RE
.PP
Remove a dependency:
.RS
.PP
minit conf ./mylib \-\-remove zlib
.RE

.SH NOTES
The script utilizes \fBsed\fR for file manipulation. On macOS/BSD systems, it automatically adjusts for the differences in \fBsed -i\fR syntax.
